# How to request a quota increase using capacity Recommender
 
This document provides how-to steps to successfully request to us Capacity Recommender to request a quota increase in your Azure Portal, thorugh Request Access or Get Recommendations actions.  
The steps for Capacity Recommender are specific to your quotas that are located in high-demand regions. 

Get started with Azure Quotas by using Capacity Recommender in the Azure portal, to request a quota increase.

## Prerequisites

- An Azure account with an active subscription. [Create an account for free](https://azure.microsoft.com/free/?WT.mc_id=A261C142F).

## Request a quota increase

You can submit a request for a quota increase directly from My quotas. Follow the steps below to request an increase for a quota. For this example, you can select any adjustable quota in your subscription.

1. Sign in to the Azure portal, and select **Quotas** located under Azure Services. 
2. Select **My Quotas** on the left pane. Your subscription quotas will come into view. 
3. Select the Quota Name checkbox, of the quota you want to increase, then select Next.
4. When the Quota recommendations page appears, select the Show Recommendations button, then select Next
5. Select **Show Recommendations**
6.	While the quota increase process is running, you will see a message stating “We are searching for alternatives.” 
7.	When the Quota recommendations blade appears, select one of the 4 quota options available, then select Next. In this scenario, we selected Standard Dv2-Family vCPU.

    **NOTE:** Notice the Region preference default displays “Keep my current region.” You can also “search in another region” but please see if the recommendations can resolve your quota capacity issue. 

